-1d1b-5478-9383-2934565c286e" :question/math-academy-id "q-332873" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/d9103a8e40d3040b711d0bcfc8cf759d6515ba7d0ae060239d203940e4b09daf.png)\n\nA sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown above (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Which of the following could represent the trajectory starting at the point marked on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point and go along with the flow (slightly downward and to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $y$-nullcline, where the tangents are horizontal.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/146fd1dd846803a8ee5684756a1ddf92b4236b49ad3082bd2397b07eb30671aa.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues to the right and gradually turns upward.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/cf3b24d0c6249d7b60803ea62a06c160b987b2892d4e56f91f0001d276ec4838.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory keeps going to the right and slightly upward to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/58cefcb6d77335a6dd54aba7bdffdb19024fd8c6aab0659389097ba1ced6d6a0.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332873/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129bee33-7c18-5450-affe-dd710a3a75dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332873"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332941/selection/8904b22ebee4d4f3d9d27e7d6d790b69c1fbef7496bb10a94482628271b55ec6" :answer/id #uuid "3dc2c5bb-d284-58ff-822b-0acb0718930c" :answer/type :answer.typ